    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193010_216740_23373" xmi:uuid="45563007-2b84-4293-b124-f5bcfa7448ef" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551280244953_893881_96460" xmi:uuid="a7269706-cb1e-4840-baec-3f1408c50f67" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847735853_401544_98065"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only an activity property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454433778732_11385_42737" xmi:uuid="bcf61100-9c29-4296-be01-30b50fae9270" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193010_216740_23373"/>
        <body>An ActivityAssignment is an association of an Activity with product or activity data. It characterizes the role of the concepts represented with these data with respect to the activity. &lt;note&gt; This entity should not be used to represent the association of an activity with the organizations that are responsible for its execution or its management. That kind of information can be represented with instances of OrganizationOrPersonInOrganizationAssignment.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ActivityAssignment</name>
