    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193008_117706_23372" xmi:uuid="9cfcccdf-ba51-4929-b7f4-fc362f72721e" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454433544200_256848_42736" xmi:uuid="e2d40868-ff15-4dfa-8e3f-e6b50ebf1460" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193008_117706_23372"/>
        <body>An Activity is an identification of the occurrence of an action that has taken place, is taking place, or is expected to take place in the future. The procedure executed during that Activity is identified with the ActivityMethod that is referred to by the ChosenMethod attribute. &lt;example&gt; Change, distilling, design, a process to drill a hole, and a task such as training someone, are examples of activities.&lt;/example&gt; &lt;note&gt; The items that are affected by an Activity may be identified within an instance of ActivityAssignment.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551271239677_596062_94220" xmi:uuid="ea1bf468-0a83-4628-bfa4-9b342816e9fb" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847735853_401544_98065"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only an activity property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Activity</name>
