    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193011_460713_23376" xmi:uuid="e9be569d-dfc4-4422-a4ce-bef10a76a700" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_271a0567_1551279092854_329796_95719" xmi:uuid="b87ad438-c7bc-4d4a-863f-0774e7139db2" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement href="../CommonResources/CommonResources.xmi#_18_4_1_290014c_1550847735853_401544_98065"/>
        <body>These flowports are not bound to the ARM target because only an activity property type can be assigned to it.</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1454434962901_652264_42770" xmi:uuid="cd4bf01a-0da3-49f1-96a3-3258ab603080" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193011_460713_23376"/>
        <body>An ActivityMethod is a way to carry out an Activity. &lt;note&gt; There may be more than one method for producing a required result.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;note&gt; This definition may be used to characterize a way to resolve a request for action.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>ActivityMethod</name>
